# The release signing key, in every shape it is handed around in. It is never read from the
# repository — androidApp/build.gradle.kts takes it from a property or the environment — but a
# keystore that reaches a commit is a key that has to be considered public, and the app's signature
# can never be changed afterwards without breaking every installed update path. So the pattern is
# here to make the accident impossible rather than to describe a file that belongs anywhere near.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
